+# Story RC3.6: Verified Webhooks — Resend Events + Twilio SMS
+
+**Status:** ready-for-dev
+**Epic:** RC3 (the referee collection funnel). Depends on rc3-1…rc3-5 (merged; #600 was the last).
+**Model:** `zai-coding-cn/glm-5.2` (kimi quota down this cycle; glm-5.2 proven capable across rc3-2…rc3-5).
+**Perkins:** ON (production server code + webhook signature security — the spoofed-bounce threat is load-bearing). Round runs on glm-5.2 fallback while kimi is down.
+**GitHub issue:** #548
+
+## Story
+
+> As the platform,
+> I want bounce and SMS delivery-failure signals to flow into the reference lifecycle through **signature-verified** webhooks only,
+> So that bad contact triggers the correction path — and nobody can forge a bounce to disrupt a reference check.
+
+rc3-1…rc3-5 shipped the outbound side: the SMS client + send helpers/templates (rc3-1/rc3-2), the referee form session (rc3-3), the exit routes incl. the **stop-link objection route** (rc3-4), and the cadence sweep (rc3-5). rc3-6 closes the **inbound** loop: two provider webhooks that HEAR back from Resend (email) and Twilio (SMS) and feed delivery-failure signals into the lifecycle. Signature verification is the whole point — an unverified webhook must change nothing (no spoofed bounce can move a row).
+
+## ⚠️ Briefing reconciliation (READ FIRST — supersedes the briefing's AC #2)
+
+The briefing's AC #2 ("inbound STOP → objected" on the Twilio webhook) is **stale**. The **2026-08-08 architecture amendment** (in the amendments register of `architecture-reference-checking-v1-2026-07-29.md`) supersedes it, and rc3-4 already shipped the amended behaviour:
+
+- The Registered Alphanumeric Sender ID `RTenantry` is **one-way / outbound-only** (Twilio: alphanumeric senders cannot receive replies). An inbound SMS STOP-reply is **physically impossible** — "dead as written".
+- Objections are owned by **rc3-4's stop-link route** (`GET/POST /reference/:token/stop` → `handle_stop_post` → `apply_objection`, verified in `router.gleam:993-996` + `form_handler.gleam:1001`). That route is live and tested.
+- The **Twilio webhook's only job is delivery-status callbacks** (SMS delivery failure → `awaiting_correction`, AD-7). It does NOT handle STOP.
+
+**This story therefore does NOT build inbound STOP→objected.** That is done (rc3-4). This story builds the two delivery-event webhooks. ✅ **CONFIRMED at clarify (2026-08-12):** the amendment wins — Twilio webhook = delivery callbacks only.
+
+## Scope (what THIS story owns — and what it does NOT)
+
+### OWNS
+1. **`server/src/reference_checks/webhooks.gleam`** (NEW) — the two webhook handlers + the shared pipeline (verify signature → parse → idempotency claim → guarded transition → audit → ack). Mirror the `inbound_email/inbound_handler.handle_webhook` shape and the rc3-4 `apply_objection` "guarded UPDATE first, evidence/audit only if it returned a row" discipline.
+2. **Resend webhook** — `POST /api/v1/webhooks/resend-events`: svix-verified (reuse `inbound_email/svix.gleam` VERBATIM — `extract_headers` + `verify_signature`). Actionable events: `email.bounced`, `email.complaint`, `email.failed`/delivery-failure → guarded transition to `awaiting_correction` (AD-7). `delivered`/`opened`/`clicked` → 200 ack, no state change. Invalid/missing svix signature → 401, **no state mutates**, Sentry capture (AD-15, NFR-RC4).
+3. **Twilio webhook** — `POST /api/v1/webhooks/twilio-sms`: `X-Twilio-Signature`-verified (NEW verifier, see #5). Actionable statuses: `failed`, `undelivered` (SMS delivery failure) → guarded transition to `awaiting_correction` (AD-7). `queued`/`sent`/`delivered` → 200 ack, no state change. Invalid/missing signature → 403 (Twilio convention), **no state mutates**, Sentry (AD-15).
+4. **Guarded transition to `awaiting_correction`** (AD-7/AD-14) — a NEW `sql/mark_awaiting_correction.sql`: `UPDATE reference_call SET status='awaiting_correction', terminal_reason=$2, next_attempt_at=NULL, updated_at=now() WHERE id=$1 AND status IN ('queued','contact_initiated') RETURNING id::text`. Zero rows = already terminal/already-awaiting (sticky + idempotent in one, AD-14). `next_attempt_at` NULL stops the sweep re-sending the bad contact (rc3-5's cadence query excludes NULL-`next_attempt_at` rows). **The webhook never sends anything** (AD-14.4: the sweep owns every send).
+5. **Twilio signature verifier** (NEW) — `server/src/notification/twilio_webhook.gleam` (lives with `sms_client`'s Twilio config): HMAC-SHA256(auth_token, `url + sorted-params`) → base64, constant-time compare via `crypto.secure_compare` against `X-Twilio-Signature`. Construct the signed URL from `TWILIO_STATUS_CALLBACK_BASE_URL` + `status_callback_path` ("/webhooks/twilio-sms", the FIXED const in `sms_client.gleam:34` — do not rename, it is a live contract) + the form-encoded params in the exact order Twilio signs them. Read `auth_token` from `config.twilio` (`TwilioConfig.auth_token`); if `Disabled` (no keys), **reject** the webhook (cannot verify → AD-15 forbids the state-mutation path). Reference: [Twilio: Request Validation](https://www.twilio.com/docs/usage/webhooks/webhooks-security).
+6. **Idempotency** (NFR-RC5 / re-delivery) — NEW table `processed_reference_webhook_event(event_id TEXT, source TEXT NOT NULL, created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(), PRIMARY KEY(source, event_id))` + NEW `sql/claim_webhook_event.sql`: `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (source, event_id) DO NOTHING RETURNING event_id` (the Stripe `claim_stripe_event.sql` / `processed_stripe_event` pattern). Zero rows = already processed → 200 ack, stand down. Event id = Resend `svix-id`-derived event id / Resend event id; Twilio `MessageSid` + `SmsSid` + status (Twilio re-delivers the same status callback).
+7. **Bounce → row mapping** — NEW `sql/find_reference_call_by_send_ref.sql`: look up the row by the **provider message id** (Resend email id / Twilio MessageSid), which the sweep (rc3-5) stored as the `detail` field of a `delivered` entry in the `attempts` jsonb (`attempts @> $1::jsonb` with `{"outcome":"delivered","detail":"<id>"}`). **Fallback**: effective contact (`contact_email`/`corrected_email` for Resend `to`; `contact_phone`/`corrected_phone` for Twilio `To`) scoped to non-terminal rows — covers the crash-mid-tick edge where the id isn't appended yet. A contact not on any live row → 200 ack, no state change, no crash.
+8. **Audit** (AD-16) — on a real transition (guarded UPDATE returned a row), write `audit_log.create_system(entity_type: "reference_call", entity_id: row.id, action: "reference_correction_requested", ...)` (the rc3-4 `form_handler.gleam:739` pattern).
+9. **Router wiring** — add the two arms to `router.gleam` next to the existing `["api","v1","webhooks","inbound-email"]` / `["api","v1","webhooks","stripe"]` arms (router.gleam:871-874).
+10. **In-app `reference_awaiting_correction` notification** (clarify ruling Q3=B2) — NEW `notify_reference_awaiting_correction` in `notification/notification_dispatch.gleam` + migration `ALTER TYPE notification_type ADD VALUE IF NOT EXISTS 'reference_awaiting_correction'`. Creates the in-app notification row ONLY (mirrors `dispatch_reference_notification` but SKIPS `maybe_send_email` — no realtime email, no digest change). Fires after the guarded transition returns a row (exactly-once). `entity_id` = the vacancy (join reference_call → application → vacancy; mirrors how `notify_reference_unreachable` scopes to the vacancy panel). The landlord sees it via the bell + dashboard; RC4.3's correction UI is where they act.
+
+### Does NOT own (deferred / sibling stories)
+- **Inbound STOP → objected** — DONE in rc3-4 (stop-link route). The 2026-08-08 amendment removed it from the Twilio webhook. **Do not rebuild it.**
+- **The correction FLOW** (landlord edits the contact inline, re-triggers the invite) → **RC4.3**. Decision A1 in the `reference_call` migration is explicit: NO `correction_token` column; correction is **landlord-driven in v1** (FR-RC8). rc3-5 deferred "applicant correction email + re-queue → RC3.6/RC4.3" — confirm RC4.3 at clarify (#2 open question). rc3-6 only sets `awaiting_correction` + audit + makes the status landlord-visible.
+- **Correction-exhaustion terminal** (`awaiting_correction → unreachable`) → RC4.3 (needs a correction-timeout SLA the arch does not specify).
+- **Email/digest for `awaiting_correction`** — rc3-6 writes the in-app `reference_awaiting_correction` notification (clarify ruling B2) but sends NO email: no realtime (avoids spam if several refs bounce), and no digest change (the existing daily digest is `ai_complete`-only — extending it was offered as B1, deferred as out of scope). The correction UI surfacing + action is RC4.3.
+- **Fraud-signal computation** (`referee_contact_invalid`) → rc3-7. (rc3-6 may stamp the `terminal_reason` slug rc3-7 reads, but does not compute the signal.)
+- **Resend flagged-reply → objected** (the email-reply objection channel) — separate; not in this story's events (bounce/complaint/failure only).
+
+## Acceptance Criteria (BDD — from epic RC3.6 + arch AD-7/14/15/16, NFR-RC4/5, FR-RC18)
+
+**AC1 — Resend webhook: verified bounce/complaint/failure → awaiting_correction (AD-7)**
+> **Given** `POST /api/v1/webhooks/resend-events`
+> **When** a svix-verified `email.bounced` / `email.complaint` / delivery-failure event arrives for a referee contact on a live (`queued`/`contact_initiated`) row
+> **Then** the row moves to `awaiting_correction` via a guarded UPDATE (`WHERE status IN ('queued','contact_initiated')`), `next_attempt_at` is NULL'd (sweep won't re-send the bad contact), `terminal_reason` is stamped (e.g. `email_bounced`/`email_complaint`/`delivery_failed`), an AD-16 `reference_correction_requested` audit row is written, and a `reference_awaiting_correction` in-app notification is created (no email)
+> **And** the handler responds 200
+
+**AC2 — Twilio webhook: verified delivery-failure → awaiting_correction (AD-7)**
+> **Given** `POST /api/v1/webhooks/twilio-sms`
+> **When** an `X-Twilio-Signature`-verified callback arrives with `MessageStatus` `failed` or `undelivered` for a referee contact on a live row
+> **Then** the same correction path applies (guarded `awaiting_correction` + NULL `next_attempt_at` + `terminal_reason` + audit)
+> **And** the handler responds 200 (Twilio expects a 2xx ack or it retries)
+
+**AC3 — Signature verification is load-bearing (AD-15, NFR-RC4) — REQUIRED TEST**
+> **Given** a request to EITHER webhook with an invalid, malformed, or missing signature (and, for Twilio, a stale/future-tolerant timestamp outside the replay window)
+> **When** the webhook receives it
+> **Then** NO state mutates, NO audit row is written, NO idempotency claim is consumed, the request is rejected (Resend: 401; Twilio: 403), and the verification failure is captured to Sentry
+> **And** a wrong-secret signature fails (`crypto.secure_compare`, constant-time)
+
+**AC4 — Idempotent re-delivery (NFR-RC5) — REQUIRED TEST**
+> **Given** a verified event is processed (transition applied, audit written, idempotency row claimed)
+> **When** the SAME event id is re-delivered (Resend/Twilio both retry)
+> **Then** `claim_webhook_event` returns zero rows → the handler responds 200 and does NOTHING (no double-transition, no duplicate audit)
+
+**AC5 — Sticky terminals survive out-of-order events (AD-14, NFR-RC5) — REQUIRED TEST**
+> **Given** a row already terminal (`objected` from rc3-4's stop-link, `form_completed`, `unreachable`, `manual_recorded`, `failed`) or already `awaiting_correction`
+> **When** a bounce/delivery-failure arrives for it
+> **Then** the guarded UPDATE returns 0 rows → the handler stands down (no audit, no objection-evidence row); an `objected` row stays `objected` (a bounce after a stop-link changes nothing — the DPC failure AD-6 exists to prevent)
+
+**AC6 — Route registration (the rc3-3/-rc3-4 lesson; field-note "wrong mechanism" + "registry-omission blocker" warnings)**
+> **Given** the two new webhook routes (`/webhooks/resend-events`, `/webhooks/twilio-sms` — TOP-LEVEL `/webhooks/*`, NOT `/api/v1/webhooks/*`, per arch §7.2 + the fixed `sms_client.status_callback_path`)
+> **When** a request arrives
+> **Then** they get a NEW CSRF arm `["webhooks", ..] -> True` in `auth/csrf.gleam` (the existing `["api","v1","webhooks",..]` prefix does NOT cover the top-level family — caught by verifying each registry against disk; a missing arm 403s the route, the rc3-3 lesson); they are NOT in `is_public_path` (rely on Cloudflare X-RT-Secret, same as the existing webhooks — no arm); `redact_token_route` does NOT apply (no path token — no arm); and both arms are wired in `router.gleam`
+> **And** this is DOCUMENTED in the PR's Decisions & rationale
+
+**AC7 — Unrecognized contact / no-op posture (rc3-2 doctrine)**
+> **Given** a verified event for a contact NOT on any live reference_call row (e.g. a co-nudge bounce for the APPLICANT's email, or a contact from an already-archived application)
+> **When** the webhook processes it
+> **Then** it responds 200, mutates nothing, and never crashes or captures to Sentry (expected, not a failure — the rc3-2 no-op doctrine)
+> **And** with Twilio `Disabled` (no keys), a Twilio callback (which in practice never arrives when no sends happened) is rejected as unverifiable, not crashed
+
+**AC8 — In-app `reference_awaiting_correction` notification (clarify Q3=B2) — REQUIRED TEST**
+> **Given** a verified event triggers a real transition (guarded UPDATE returns a row)
+> **When** the handler finishes
+> **Then** exactly ONE `reference_awaiting_correction` in-app notification row exists for the row's vacancy (entity_id = vacancy), created via `notify_reference_awaiting_correction`
+> **And** NO email is sent (no realtime call, no digest change) — the bell + dashboard surface it; a re-delivered event does NOT create a second notification (idempotency + the guarded UPDATE gate it)
+
+**AC9 — Build/test green**
+> `make format && make test && make build` green; `make test-server` (unit + the new webhook tests) green. No `let assert` in production code. No em-dashes in any user-facing copy (RT CI ban) — webhooks are machine-facing, so this is a no-op but stated for completeness.
+
+## Dev Notes (load-bearing decisions — also the PR's "Decisions & rationale")
+
+1. **Briefing AC #2 is stale; the amendment wins.** The 2026-08-08 amendment (amendments register) + rc3-4's shipped stop-link route + Twilio's documented one-way alphanumeric sender prove the inbound STOP→objected path is dead. The Twilio webhook does delivery callbacks only. This is confirmed against disk (router.gleam:993-996 stop route; sms_client.gleam:29-34 forward-ref const) and vendor docs. **Rejected:** building inbound STOP handling — it would be dead code (no inbound SMS possible) and duplicate rc3-4. (Open question #1 — confirm.)
+
+2. **Correction FLOW is RC4.3, not rc3-6.** Decision A1 in `20260731222000_create_reference_call.sql`: "NO `correction_token` column — correction and substitution are landlord-driven in v1". FR-RC8: landlord confirms details with the applicant, edits the slot's trio inline (audit-logged), saving re-triggers. rc3-6 only DETECTS bad contact and sets `awaiting_correction` (the state the correction UI reads). rc3-5 already excludes `awaiting_correction` from the cadence (NULL `next_attempt_at`). (Open question #2 — confirm RC4.3.)
+
+3. **In-app notification only (clarify Q3=B2).** The user wants the landlord to learn a ref needs correction, but NOT via spammy per-bounce emails. Decision: add `reference_awaiting_correction` to the `notification_type` enum + a `notify_reference_awaiting_correction` that creates the in-app row ONLY (skips `maybe_send_email` — no realtime email). NO digest change (the existing daily digest is `ai_complete`-only; extending it was B1, deferred as out of scope). The landlord sees the bell badge + dashboard status; RC4.3's correction UI is where they act. Exactly-once: fires only when the guarded UPDATE returns a row (a re-bounce / idempotent re-delivery creates no second notification). `entity_id` = vacancy (mirror `notify_reference_unreachable`).
+
+4. **Idempotency = dedicated processed-events table (Stripe pattern), not the inbound_email ON-CONFLICT pattern.** Two webhook sources (Resend + Twilio) → one table `processed_reference_webhook_event(event_id, source, created_at)` with `PRIMARY KEY(source, event_id)` (a Resend id and a Twilio sid could theoretically collide; the composite key is safe). `claim_webhook_event` returns 0 rows on re-delivery. Event id: Resend — the event's unique id (svix payloads carry `evt_<id>`; fall back to `svix-id` if absent); Twilio — `MessageSid` + `MessageStatus` (Twilio re-sends the same status; `MessageSid` alone would dedup the whole callback sequence, so key on sid+status). **Claim BEFORE the transition** so a crash mid-handler doesn't double-apply; the guarded UPDATE is the second layer of exactly-once.
+
+5. **Guarded transition reuses the AD-14 discipline, not the generic `update_reference_call_status`.** `update_reference_call_status.sql` takes ONE expected pre-state; a bounce can arrive on `queued` or `contact_initiated`. A dedicated `mark_awaiting_correction.sql` guarding `status IN ('queued','contact_initiated')` is cleaner and gives sticky-terminal + idempotency in one UPDATE. `next_attempt_at` NULL is already what entering `awaiting_correction` requires (the generic query's CASE list includes it). Mirror the NULLIF/COALESCE conventions and the `::text`/`::reference_call_status` casts.
+
+6. **Bounce → row mapping: message-id primary, contact fallback.** The sweep (rc3-5) appends each send's provider id as the `detail` of a `delivered` `attempts` entry (`attempts` jsonb shape: `{at, channel, outcome, detail}`). A Resend bounce carries `email.id`; a Twilio callback carries `MessageSid`. `find_reference_call_by_send_ref.sql` matches `attempts @> $1::jsonb` first (exact, unambiguous). **Fallback** by effective contact covers the crash-mid-tick edge (send went out, sweep crashed before appending). Effective contact = `COALESCE(NULLIF(corrected_email,''), contact_email)` (AD-7 effective-contact rule, rc3-5 applies corrected ?? snapshot). Scope the fallback to non-terminal rows; if genuinely ambiguous (same email on two live rows), log a warning + act on the most recent — document this in the PR.
+
+7. **Resend `complaint` → `awaiting_correction`, NOT `objected`.** The epic AC routes bounce/complaint to the correction path. A spam complaint is arguably an objection, but the email-objection channel is the "flagged reply" path (separate, not in scope), and the epic is explicit. Stamp `terminal_reason: 'email_complaint'` so rc3-7's `referee_contact_invalid` fraud signal can read it. (Flag as a minor decision in the PR.)
+
+8. **Resend reuses `inbound_email/svix.gleam` VERBATIM.** Do NOT reinvent svix verification. `extract_headers` + `verify_signature` (HMAC-SHA256, base64 secret, `whsec_` strip, 5-min two-sided replay window, `crypto.secure_compare`). The `resend_webhook_secret` is already on `ServerConfig` (config.gleam:27). Read the raw body with `wisp.require_string_body` BEFORE verifying (the inbound_handler.gleam:48-83 pattern).
+
+9. **Twilio signature is a NEW verifier** (no existing scaffold — confirmed). It is HMAC-SHA256(auth_token, url + sorted-form-params), base64 — DIFFERENT from svix. The signed URL = `status_callback_base_url` + `status_callback_path` (no trailing slash); params are concatenated as `keyvalue` pairs in **sorted ASCII order by key** (Twilio's spec). Verify the full form body (not a subset). Use `crypto.secure_compare`. Reject on `Disabled` (no auth_token to verify with). Put it in `notification/twilio_webhook.gleam` (with the Twilio config), exposed for unit tests.
+
+10. **Route registration: verify, don't blanket-add.** The briefing + field notes say "register in all three registries", but for WEBHOOKS (no path token, Cloudflare-fronted) the truth is: CSRF covered by the existing prefix arm; `is_public_path` N/A (Cloudflare X-RT-Secret, like inbound-email/stripe); `redact_token_route` N/A (no token). Confirm each against disk in the PR. This is the field-note "WRONG MECHANISM" warning in action (2026-08-11 dream).
+
+11. **Reuse targets (do NOT reinvent):** `inbound_email/svix.gleam` (Resend sig), `payment/sql/claim_stripe_event.sql` + `processed_stripe_event` (idempotency), rc3-4 `apply_objection` (`form_handler.gleam:1018+`, the "guarded UPDATE first, evidence only on success" discipline), `audit_log.create_system` (AD-16), `response_helpers.json_error` (rejection responses), rc3-2 `send` ChannelOutcome `detail` (the message-id mapping source), rc3-5 sweep (the cadence that excludes `awaiting_correction`).
+
+## Resolved rulings (clarify, lavish session 2026-08-12 — all answered)
+
+1. **Q1 — Twilio webhook scope = A (amendment).** Delivery callbacks only (→ `awaiting_correction`); NO inbound STOP handling. rc3-4 stop-link owns objections; sender is one-way.
+2. **Q2 — Correction flow scope = A (RC4.3).** rc3-6 = webhooks only (detect → `awaiting_correction` + audit + in-app notification). The correction FLOW (landlord edits inline, re-trigger) + correction-exhaustion terminal = RC4.3.
+3. **Q3 — awaiting_correction notification = B2 (in-app only).** Add `reference_awaiting_correction` in-app notification, NO email (no realtime, no digest change). The user explicitly rejected per-row realtime email (spam) and chose in-app-only over extending the digest (B1) as simpler.
+4. **Q4 — bounce→row mapping = message-id-in-attempts primary + effective-contact fallback** (Dev Note 6). Decided by the minion (implementation detail); no user ruling needed.
+
